          "Do not assume that a 55% margin reflects an immobile base; in a district where 33% of population is African American and Hispanic combined, and where homeownership strongly predicts partisanship, any challenger who mobilizes underparticipating minority voters while maintaining credibility on homeowner concerns can move this seat into the 50-50 range within a single cycle."
