          "Avoid treating the 57% result as a safe majority: recognize instead that this is a working-class coalition held together by perceptions about economic delivery rather than strong partisan identity, making it vulnerable to any candidate who takes the opposition's economic concerns more seriously or delivers more convincingly on working-class priorities."
