          { name: "Ignoring the 21.1% Renter Constituency", tag: "avoid", why: "While homeowners dominate at 78.9%, one-fifth of the district consists of renters—likely a mix of younger adults and fixed-income seniors for whom housing stability, affordability, and neighborhood livability are direct economic concerns. A campaign that focuses exclusively on homeowner property tax issues and ignores renter-specific concerns around affordability, displacement, and neighborhood change will miss an opportunity to consolidate younger voters who may otherwise align with Democratic messaging on economic mobility and housing security." }
