          "Activate college-educated voters on governance competence and fiscal stewardship: the 38.2% college attainment rate in a Republican district signals a constituency that evaluates on institutional performance and evidence-based policy, not partisan identity alone—demonstrate concrete local governance results on budget management and service delivery.",
          "Do not treat 61% as a structural majority: the combination of older fixed-income exposure and college-educated voter independence means the margin is held by active alignment, not demographic destiny—any candidate who consolidates only the existing base while ignoring the 39% opposition will find it mobilized in a competitive cycle.",
          "Engage the 21.1% renter constituency on housing stability and affordability: while homeowners dominate, one-fifth of the district is renters, likely younger adults or fixed-income seniors for whom housing costs and neighborhood stability are direct economic concerns that deserve specific legislative attention."
