          "Do not campaign this 56-44 district as though the margin is stable without active constituent engagement on the college-educated and renter majorities' real economic concerns — the opposition's 44% reflects material policy disagreement, not inherited partisanship, and can be moved by candidates who offer credible economic solutions."
