          "Prevent professional-class defection by demonstrating that Democratic governance delivers measurable results on the issues that matter to affluent, educated voters: the 55-45 margin is narrow enough that a 3-4 point swing among professionals in the next cycle could flip the seat to Republican control.",
          "Engage the Asian and Black professional communities as integrated constituents within the broader affluent professional base, not as separate demographic outreach targets; these voters share economic interests and quality-of-life concerns with white professionals and evaluate candidates on competence and delivery, not racial positioning.",
          "Avoid any framing that treats homeowners or property-tax-paying professionals as obstacles to progressive governance; in a district this affluent and educated, the incumbent's coalition is built on professional-class voters whose tax burden and property values are material concerns — not resentment masquerading as policy."
