          "Address the cost-of-living reality directly: $138K income is high, but housing costs in affluent urban/suburban markets are rising faster than incomes, and younger professionals renting (21.9% renter rate) face real affordability pressure; avoiding this issue cedes ground to Republican messaging on regulatory burden and supply-side constraints.",
          "Defend against tax-fairness critique by documenting the specific public services—schools, infrastructure, healthcare—that justify the tax burden; professional-class voters are not anti-tax by ideology, but they demand transparency on what their tax dollars deliver.",
          "Manage the 38% opposition by understanding whether it concentrates among high-income business owners responsive to regulatory/tax messaging or among ideological conservatives; targeted messaging to business-community swing voters differs fundamentally from consolidation of the progressive base."
