          "Engage the ~48% demographic gap with specificity: whether this represents AIAN, multiracial, or other communities, their presence at nearly half the district's population demands authentic constituent attention and cultural fluency, not assumption that the Democratic margin automatically captures their interests.",
          "Defend and expand the material benefits Democrats have delivered: if the current representative has secured Medicaid expansion, increased minimum wage, rental assistance, or other concrete economic relief, run on results — and if not, explain why and commit to what comes next.",
          "Assume a Republican challenger will offer their own economic messaging: a 65-35 margin in a working-poor district is not a fortress; it is a consolidated preference for Democratic economic positioning that can be tested by a credible Republican offer on jobs, housing, or healthcare costs that appears more concrete and achievable."
