          "Avoid treating 55% as a safe Democratic floor or 45% as a stable Republican ceiling; in an affluent suburban district where college-educated professionals are actively reassessing their partisan alignments, a 55-45 margin is genuinely competitive and vulnerable to candidate quality, specific issue performance, and whether voters perceive government is delivering on healthcare, infrastructure, and services — not inherited loyalty."
