          "Demonstrate visible constituent service and economic delivery: the 75% margin is held by effective consolidation of the white homeowner base, but that consolidation requires evidence that the incumbent is producing outcomes on the issues working-class households evaluate — not just partisan messaging.",
          "Engage the multiethnic composition of the working-class base: the 12.65% Black and 8.21% Hispanic populations are part of the 75% Republican coalition and have specific economic needs around workforce development, small-business support, and healthcare access that deserve explicit attention rather than being absorbed into generic working-class messaging.",
          "Do not treat 75% as a structural ceiling — treat it as a margin that requires active defense: any incumbent who consolidates existing support and ignores the opposition's driving concerns risks finding a credible challenger who addresses housing or healthcare costs and closes the margin to 68-72% in the next cycle."
