          { name: "Defaulting to Partisan Rhetoric Over Constituent Problem-Solving", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district where 56.1% of adults have college degrees and median income is $148,172, voters have the information resources and the material security to evaluate candidates on competence and whether their specific problems are being addressed, not on abstract partisan positioning. An incumbent whose messaging focuses on partisan attack rather than on concrete accomplishments in school funding, infrastructure quality, tax management, or constituent service will find that message underperforms with an educated, prosperous constituency that has learned to expect—and demand—results. This district rewards the candidate who demonstrates competence and constituent focus; it punishes one who relies on partisan tribalism." }
