          "Lead with competent fiscal management and constituent service delivery: affluent, educated homeowners at $148k income and 56.1% college attainment evaluate on whether government is delivering efficiently, not on conservative ideology—detail specific accomplishments in school funding, infrastructure, and local service quality.",
          "Engage the 28.5% nonwhite constituency (Hispanic, Black, Asian, and Native American combined) with specific attention to their economic mobility, healthcare access, and representation in local decision-making; at these income levels, professional minorities are acutely aware of whether they are being served and heard.",
          "Monitor demographic shifts actively: with median age at 40.4 and high education attainment, the district is likely attracting younger professionals whose economic concerns (housing costs, student debt, childcare) and values (diversity, climate, fiscal responsibility) may diverge from the current homeowner-dominant coalition—a credible challenger addressing younger professional concerns could shift the margin significantly."
