          "Engage the Hispanic community (14.84%) and AIAN residents (3.7% gap) with specific constituent attention to their economic mobility, healthcare, and education needs; in a district where the Anglo working-class majority dominates the partisan story, other communities can become invisible to representation despite being present and having material needs.",
          "Avoid treating 76% as a safe floor: the combination of modest income, limited education, and high renter rate (30.5%) creates a constituency that will punish incumbents who fail to deliver on economic outcomes — any candidate who campaigns on partisan loyalty alone while working-class households experience wage stagnation is building electoral vulnerability for the next cycle.",
