          { name: "Partisan Polarization Frames That Ignore Local Economic Reality", tag: "avoid", why: "NC-HD-89's 77.4% white, 81.3% homeowner, $69,738 income profile does not naturally sort into red-team or blue-team identities — it is a constituency that evaluates on whether government is delivering practical results on the economic concerns that matter to their daily lives. Any candidate whose primary communication strategy relies on national partisan narratives rather than specific solutions to property taxes, healthcare costs, housing affordability, and local infrastructure will find that strategy less effective than one grounded in the material concerns of the district's actual households. The 24% opposition exists partly because some voters in this district have concluded the current representation is not addressing their concerns with sufficient specificity — a persuadable finding if the alternative offers a credible, locally-grounded program." }
