          "NC-HD-91 is a consolidating Republican district where Hall's 67-33 margin masks a constituency profile that should produce substantially higher Republican performance by national benchmarks. The district's median age of 45.1, median household income of $62,413, and college attainment of only 21.8% — the lowest in this comparative set — define a working-class to lower-middle-class, older, asset-holding homeowner base (79.8% ownership) that typically votes Republican at 70%+ in North Carolina state house races. The 67% result suggests Hall is holding the Anglo homeowner base but underperforming among non-white voters relative to what a demographically similar district would normally deliver. The 3.4% demographic gap (76.23% white + 12.54% Black + 7.6% Hispanic + 0.24% Asian = 96.61%, leaving 3.39% unaccounted for) is modest compared to other districts but still represents roughly 1,800-2,000 constituents whose voting behavior or turnout patterns are not fully visible in the partisan result.",
