          "Avoid taking the 67% as a durable floor: a 34-point margin is comfortable but not impregnable in a district where 20%+ is non-white and working-class voters evaluate on material outcomes, not inherited loyalty — sustained attention to constituent services and economic messaging is required to hold the seat against a credible challenger."
