          { name: "Treating Four Demographic Communities as Politically Equivalent", tag: "avoid", why: "NC-HD-92's four major demographic communities (35.84% Black, 29.1% White, 21.42% Hispanic, 8.12% Asian) are not of equivalent political or demographic weight — the 57.26% Black and Hispanic majority is the coalition foundation, while the 37.22% White and Asian minority is the coalition partner. A representative who distributes governance attention, rhetoric, and resource allocation as though all four communities are equal in size or political weight will appear to the 57% as if their priorities are being subordinated to minority community preferences — a perception that invites primary challenge or coalition fracture. Coalition leadership requires explicit clarity about who the majority is and what they need." }
