          { name: "Taking the Education-Professional Base for Granted", tag: "avoid", why: "The 29.6% college attainment and $71,669 median household income signal an educated, economically stable base that should be Democratic-aligned — but education and income do not guarantee turnout or candidate loyalty if economic concerns are not being addressed. College-educated voters evaluate on school quality (for families with children), student debt relief, professional employment opportunities, and housing affordability. An incumbent who assumes this base will show up for a Democratic candidate without actively addressing these material concerns is making a critical strategic error. A well-positioned challenger with credible positions on education quality, debt relief, and housing affordability can persuade this constituency to split their ballot or stay home." }
