          "Recognize that 56% is a contested margin, not a secure majority: in a district this affluent and educated, candidate quality, competence perception, and responsiveness to constituent concerns matter more than partisan label — any incumbent or challenger who campaigns assuming 56% represents a comfortable hold is underestimating the district's actual political fluidity."
