          "Lead with housing affordability and renter-specific policy: at 39.1% renter rate and $54,428 median income, NC-SD-4 households are facing direct housing pressure that state legislation can address through tenant protection, rent regulation, or housing development incentives — this is the issue most likely to mobilize Black renters and Hispanic working-class voters simultaneously.",
