          { name: "Positioning Minority Communities as Secondary Constituencies", tag: "avoid", why: "With 36.37% Hispanic and Black population, NC-SD-12 is genuinely multiethnic, not a White-majority district with minority communities on the margins. Any candidate who campaigns this seat as though the White working-class vote is the primary constituency and minorities are a secondary consideration will find that framing politically ineffective and strategically limiting. Material governance on housing, healthcare, education, and economic opportunity for these communities is not a secondary issue — it is the direct constituent service obligation of a representative in a district where more than one-third of the population is Hispanic or Black." }
