          { name: "Assuming Hispanic Community Incorporation Without Specific Engagement", tag: "avoid", why: "At 19.78% and growing, the Hispanic community is a significant constituency that cannot be absorbed into generic 'diversity' or 'progressive coalition' messaging. Specific attention to workplace conditions, immigration policy, small-business support, and Spanish-language accessibility distinguishes genuine engagement from token inclusion. A legislator who assumes Hispanic voters are automatically locked into a 73% coalition without demonstrating specific policy wins or visible constituent service on issues that matter to this community will find that support erodes if a challenger offers more concrete engagement." }
