          "Engage the Black and Hispanic communities as the demographic foundation of the coalition at 37.9% combined: criminal justice reform, educational equity, healthcare access in minority communities, and economic development opportunities are not secondary issues but the primary concerns that generate and sustain Democratic turnout. Treat these communities as core constituencies requiring active constituent service and specific policy responsiveness, not as reliable voters to be taken for granted.",
          "Address the renter constituency with particular strategic focus: at 32.2% renter rate in a $61,309 income district, housing cost burden is an acute economic issue for a substantial portion of the electorate. Any credible challenger will lead on housing affordability; an incumbent must demonstrate concrete action on rent stabilization, tenant protections, and affordable housing development rather than rhetorical commitment.",
          "Recognize that 38% opposition in a working-class district is not a stable minority but a persuadable constituency: voters at this income level are evaluating whether government is functioning for them across education, healthcare, and economic opportunity. Incumbent vulnerability emerges when opposition candidates successfully reframe the race around government dysfunction or insufficient delivery on material concerns — preventing this requires demonstrating tangible results on the issues that structure working-class family economics."
