          "Monitor college-educated voter sentiment on cultural issues: the 41.8% college attainment in a Republican district means this is not a constituency driven by cultural grievance, but rather one evaluating whether the candidate can balance cultural conservatism with pragmatic governance and respect for diversity. Positioning that alienates college-educated voters or relies on culture-war framing risks triggering the educational polarization that has made suburban seats vulnerable.",
          "Treat 63% as a working margin, not a safe base: in a district this prosperous and educated, the 37% Democratic opposition represents genuine professional-class voters who are persuadable and are actively being organized. Any incumbent who campaigns as though 63% is a comfortable hold without active engagement of swing voters in the college-educated and Hispanic professional communities will find the margin compressed in the next cycle."
