          "Lead with older homeowner economic security: at 44.4 median age, $56,023 income, and 75.5% homeownership, this is a constituency acutely concerned with property tax fairness, Medicare sustainability, and rural hospital viability; a representative must demonstrate concrete delivery on these issues or risk credible Democratic challenge.",
          "Identify and hold the 21% opposition actively — understand whether it concentrates among younger adults (harder to reach), renters (easier to target), or specific rural communities with localized grievances; the margin to a Democratic challenger is entirely contained in moving that 21% and suppressing Republican turnout among discouraged older voters.",
          "Monitor demographic drift in adjacent precincts: the 2.7% gap in reported demographics and the district's older profile suggest aging-in-place without replacement by younger families; if the median age increases further and college attainment remains at 17.2%, the district becomes even more dependent on high incumbent personal approval to offset lower aggregate turnout among a shrinking younger cohort."
