          "Lead with the college-educated, younger, diverse constituency's material concerns: housing affordability for the 47.8% renter population, public education funding and quality, healthcare access, and economic mobility in a high-income district where significant portions of residents feel economically squeezed despite aggregate affluence.",
          "Build explicit coalition maintenance with the Black (23.42%) and Hispanic (18.06%) communities—together representing 41.48% of the district—through specific policy engagement on economic opportunity, criminal justice, and community investment; these communities are large enough to determine outcomes but can become overlooked if the incumbent focuses only on the white majority.",
          "Recognize that 56.9% college attainment means this constituency expects sophisticated governance and specific policy competence; abstract partisan rhetoric and generic conservative or progressive positioning will underperform with voters who evaluate candidates primarily on demonstrated understanding of complex issues affecting their lives."
