          "Address healthcare access and cost as an economic justice issue, not partisan talking point: the 39.2 median age and 26.6% college attainment profile suggests a working-age constituency with healthcare costs as a direct household budget concern; candidates who speak fluently about Medicaid, rural hospital viability, prescription drug costs, and insurance affordability will resonate more credibly than abstract market rhetoric.",
