          { name: "Ignoring the 27% Opposition as Unwinnable", tag: "avoid", why: "A 27% Democratic share in NC-SD-44 is not negligible—it represents roughly 19,000-22,000 voters depending on turnout, and it suggests a constituency that already prefers an alternative to the incumbent. In a district where economic anxiety is the primary swing variable and where a 15-20 point shift would require only a modest erosion of the Republican base plus mobilization of the opposition, treating the 27% as permanently lost and focusing exclusively on consolidating the 73% is strategically incomplete. Understanding specifically who the 27% are and what would move them is essential to defending the seat." }
