          "Monitor minority voter engagement and consolidation in the 3.2% demographic gap and existing 7.14% Hispanic/Latino and 4.54% Black communities; a shift in how these voters perceive representation could narrow the 30-point margin materially, particularly if a credible Democratic challenger emerges with an economic message.",
          "Avoid treating 65-35 as a permanent foundation; the 35% opposition is substantial in a Republican state and reflects real voter dissatisfaction. Any incumbent who consolidates only the existing Republican base without addressing the economic concerns driving opposition will find the margin vulnerable in a competitive cycle.",
