          "Recognize that 36% opposition in a district this conservative is not normal partisan noise — it represents genuine frustration among a constituency that should, by demographic profile alone, be more Republican; understanding whether that frustration is driven primarily by healthcare costs, property tax burden, rural service decline, or some combination is essential to holding the seat."
